331-332	40,1190,900,1898 - 846,1185,905,1420 - 822,1530,905,1900	331. Leaf, and 332. Flowers of Wild Geranium.	On the left, 331, a large leaf of Wild Geranium deeply parted into toothed lobes on a long stalk; on the right, 332, a flowering stem with an open five-petalled flower, buds and a young fruit.
333	818,1560,946,1885	333. Stamens and pistil.	The stamens standing round the pistil in the cup of the calyx, their filaments joined at the bottom, with the styles rising above.
334	938,1422,1172,1878	334. Fruit bursting.	The ripe fruit bursting: the five styles splitting away from the long central beak and curling up, each carrying a small seed-pod at its tip.
335	857,1230,978,1394	335. Seed.	A single oval seed with a netted, roughened coat.
336	1037,1245,1172,1398	336 Same, cut across.	The seed cut across, showing the folded embryo inside its coat.
